      "title": "ArchiMate models — every view, element and relationship a node",
      "description": "ArchiMate models as knowledge-graph content: how an instance declares the Archi models it holds, what the `archimate` subgraph gives every model, view, element and relationship (an IRI, a thin page, and every view drawn as SVG from the model's own diagram), how to version the models, how to wire them into a folio's staging build and navbar, and why no Java, no Archi CLI and no Archi HTML report is ever part of the pipeline. Read before adding, publishing or rendering an `.archimate` file, before citing an ArchiMate element from prose, and before reaching for Archi's own tooling in CI.",
